/*  An actor: a named rabbit, one mailbox, several kinds of message, and a reply.

    An actor needs five things — an identity, a mailbox, more than one kind of message, a
    guarantee that every kind is handled, and a way to be told to stop. Cufet has all five
    already, and this program is the whole of it. Nothing here is an actor feature; it is the
    channel, the union and `Judge` doing what they each already do.

    ★★ THE ONE THAT SURPRISES PEOPLE: **a channel can carry a union**, so one mailbox takes
    several kinds of message. `Judge` then dispatches on what arrived, and its coverage is
    PROVED — leave a kind unhandled and the program is refused before it runs. That is the pair
    that removes the need for a select.

    ⚠ Go and Occam need a guarded multi-input wait (`select`, `ALT`) for exactly this job,
    because their channels carry ONE type: an actor there listens on several channels at once
    and takes whichever speaks first. The reasoning does not transfer. Cufet puts the alternation
    in the TYPE rather than in the wait, and a union channel with a total `Judge` is the same
    expressive power with the exhaustiveness checked. See DESIGN, *Memory and concurrency*.

    ★ A worker like this KEEPS STATE across messages — `total` lives above the loop and survives
    every turn. That is why the loop is written inside an ordinary task rather than the task
    itself being made to repeat.

    ★ Shutdown needs no message kind of its own: `Close inbox` makes the next delivery void, and
    the `While` ends. The worker then closes `replies`, which is how the reader below learns that
    no more answers are coming. A closed channel is the end-of-stream signal in both directions.
*/

Pull a rabbit as hopper.
    Define inbox as a channel of (number or text).
    Define replies as a channel of number.

    Have hopper start a task as ledger:
        Define total as 0.
        Define message as the delivery from inbox.
        While message is not void, repeat:
            Define current as message but void is 0.
            Judge current, where it is:
                A number, increment total by it.
                A text, send total through replies.
            Done.
            The message becomes the delivery from inbox.
        Done.
        Close replies.
    Done.

    Send 5 through inbox.
    Send 7 through inbox.
    Send "total" through inbox.
    Send 100 through inbox.
    Send "total" through inbox.
    Close inbox.

    Define answer as the delivery from replies.
    While answer is not void, repeat:
        State "total: {answer but void is 0}".
        The answer becomes the delivery from replies.
    Done.
Done.

State "the ledger is closed".
